# Getting started

This service runs the warehouse gateway with `backend: mem`: the catalog-only
backend needs no warehouse credentials and does not execute queries. The agent
generates the caller token locally and delivers it to consumers. Its test step
checks that the gateway is serving and accepts that token.

Deployment requires an environment-managed Kubernetes secret reference for
`SWH_AUTH_TOKEN`. Bind the same secret key to every consumer's `warehouse.token`
configuration. The rendered NetworkPolicy allows only same-namespace ingress;
a policy-capable CNI is required. Anonymous access is only an explicit opt-in
when running the gateway directly for local development.
